# Print
Top level method for printing results

- **Package:** [Core](../../Core/package/Core.md)
- **Class:** [Symbol](../../Core/type/Symbol.md)
- **Aliases:** `Core$Print`
- **See also:** _undocumented_

## Description
The function `f` is responsible for printing the output prompt and for applying the [BeforePrint](../../Core/symbol/BeforePrint.md) and [AfterPrint](../../Core/symbol/AfterPrint.md) methods, if desired.

#### Consequences
At top level, whenever it is time to print an output value of type `X`, the function `f` will be called

## Examples
```macaulay2
code Thing#{Standard,Print}
```

```
o1 = /usr/share/Macaulay2/Core/robust.m2:132:25-
148:6: --source code:
Thing#{Standard,Print} = x -> (
oprompt := concatenate(interpreterDepth:"o", toString lineNumber, " = ");
save := printWidth;
if printWidth != 0 then printWidth = printWidth - #oprompt;
z := robustNet x;
wrapper := lookup(global Wrap,class x);
if wrapper =!= null then (
fun := () -> z = wrapper z;
try timelimit(printingTimeLimit, fun)
else (
alarm 0;
global debugError <- fun;
stderr << "--error or time limit reached in applying Wrap method to output; type 'debugError()' to see it" << endl << endl);
);
<< endl << oprompt << z << endl;
printWidth = save;
)
```

# benchmark
Accurate timing of execution

- **Package:** [Core](../../Core/package/Core.md)
- **Class:** [FunctionClosure](../../Core/type/FunctionClosure.md)
- **Result type:** [RR](../../Core/type/RR.md)
- **Aliases:** `Core$benchmark`
- **See also:** _undocumented_

## Description
Produces an accurate timing for the code contained in the string `s`.  The value returned is the number of seconds. The snippet of code provided will be run enough times to register meaningfully on the clock, and the garbage collector will be called beforehand.

## Parameters
- **s** — a [String](../../Core/type/String.md), a string containing Macaulay2 code

## Returns
a [RR](../../Core/type/RR.md), the number of seconds it takes to evaluate the code in s

## Examples
```macaulay2
benchmark "sqrt 2p100000"
```

```
o1 = .0003011937565882687
o1 : RR (of precision 53)
```

## Source
```m2
benchmark = (s) -> (
     n := 1;
     local firsttime;
     while (
	  s1 := concatenate("timing scan(",toString n,", iBenchmark -> (",s,";null;null))");
	  s2 := concatenate("timing scan(",toString n,", iBenchmark -> (      null;null))");
	  collectGarbage();
	  t1 := first value s1;
	  t2 := first value s2;
	  t := t1 - t2;
	  if n === 1 then firsttime = t;
	  collectGarbage();
	  -- the second timing result is better
	  value s1;
	  value s2;
	  collectGarbage();
	  t1 = first value s1;
	  t2 = first value s2;
	  t = t1 - t2;
	  t < 1 and t2 < 5)
     do (
	  n = if t > 0.01 then floor(2*n/t+.5) else 100*n;
	  );
     t = t/n;
     if firsttime > 3*t then (
	  stderr << "--warning: code being benchmarked ran longer the first time (" << firsttime << " seconds)" << endl;
	  stderr << "--         perhaps results were cached" << endl;
	  );
     t)
```

# columnate
Arrange strings in columns

- **Package:** [Core](../../Core/package/Core.md)
- **Class:** [FunctionClosure](../../Core/type/FunctionClosure.md)
- **Result type:** _undocumented_
- **Aliases:** `Core$columnate`
- **Parameters:** _undocumented_
- **Returns:** _undocumented_
- **See also:** _undocumented_

## Description
`columnate(w, s)` -- arranges the strings in the list `s` in columns, returning a [Net](../../Core/type/Net.md) suitable for output to a terminal with a linewidth of `w`.

## Examples
```macaulay2
columnate(12, characters ascii (65 .. 90))
```

```
o1 = A F K P U Z
B G L Q V
C H M R W
D I N S X
E J O T Y
```

## Source
```m2
columnate = (wid,items) -> (
     lens := apply(items,i -> #i);
     ncols := (wid+1) // (max lens + 1);
     if ncols === 0 then ncols = 1;
     nrows := (# items + ncols - 1)//ncols;
     local newcols;
     local newrows;
     while (
	  ncols < # items and (
	       newcols = ncols+1;
	       newrows = (# items + ncols - 1)//newcols;
	       wid >= newcols - 1 + sum apply(pack(newrows, lens), max)
	       )
	  ) do (
	  ncols = newcols;
	  nrows = newrows;
	  );
     horizontalJoin between(" ", apply(pack(nrows,items), col -> stack col)))
```

